# Every shape the TypeTable can hold, written as a field so the golden reads
# as a list of them.
#
# 'i32[]' is NOT here, since 2026-09-06, and neither is '[i32]' or
# '{i32: f64}' since 2026-09-10. Record 0022 makes all three written form for
# a class of the standard library and record 0025's pass rewrites them before
# this phase runs, so what a field spelled that way holds is a named type and
# not a shape of its own. The array shape still exists -- 'new T[n]' with a
# length no constant evaluation can read builds one -- it just cannot be
# written as a type any more. Their cases are in tests/sugar.
class Node:
    plain : i32
    pointer : i32*
    two : i32**
    three : i32***
    reference : i32&
    tuple : (i32, f64, bool)
    sized : i32[10]
